  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Gold is then extracted from this complex by displacement technique by using a more electropositive zinc metal.</p><p>In this method, zinc (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi></math>) acts as a reducing agent and it reduces<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Au</mi><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Au</mi></math> and itself gets oxidized from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ions which combine with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>CN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> ions and form soluble complex, sodium tetracyanozincate (II).</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Au</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>Zn</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Au</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math></p></blockquote>",
